LOOK: Cardinal Pablo Virgilio David, Bishop Colin Bagafora, Bishop Gerardo Alminaza, and Bishop Roberto Gaa join the “Trillion Peso March” rally against corruption at the People Power Monument in Quezon City. 

📷: CBCP News

@inquirerdotnet https://t.co/Q8Q9OhRwEe

A giant crocodile-shaped cake and a lechon buwaya are on display at San Pedro Square, Davao City, as the “Pray for the Philippines” rally kicks off this Sunday afternoon.

Around 100 lechon baka will also be served to attendees of the gathering, which calls for government action against corruption and the release of detained former President Rodrigo Duterte.

